      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We have $10x+2=2(5x+1)$ and $10x+6=(5x+3)(10x+2)$\nThus, $$(10x+2)(10x+6)(5x+5)=2^{3}(5x+1)(5x+3)(5x+5).\\mathrm{LHS}\\stackrel{\\text{Fermat}}{\\Longrightarrow} \\text{All factors are powers of }2\\text{ and at least one for }5.\n\\text{Therefore, the largest integer that always divides the expression} $$ \\implies\\boxed{30}.",
